f:["$","$L17",null,{"toc":[{"depth":2,"url":"#what-makes-a-build-large-in-the-way-that-matters","title":"What makes a build \"large\" in the way that matters"},{"depth":2,"url":"#why-caching-alone-runs-out","title":"Why caching alone runs out"},{"depth":2,"url":"#routing-actions-to-the-hardware-that-fits","title":"Routing actions to the hardware that fits"},{"depth":2,"url":"#special-hardware-and-what-forge-actually-knows-about-it","title":"Special hardware, and what Forge actually knows about it"},{"depth":2,"url":"#running-a-heterogeneous-fleet","title":"Running a heterogeneous fleet"},{"depth":2,"url":"#toolchains-are-the-hard-part-not-the-scheduling","title":"Toolchains are the hard part, not the scheduling"},{"depth":2,"url":"#what-a-build-like-this-looks-like-when-it-works","title":"What a build like this looks like when it works"},{"depth":2,"url":"#common-questions","title":"Common questions"}],"full":"$undefined","children":[["$","$L18",null,{"children":"Silicon and large builds"}],["$","$L19",null,{"children":"EDA flows, large C++ and LLVM trees, and ML graphs are the workloads remote execution was invented for: thousands of actions, hardware that differs from action to action, and a long tail that decides the wall clock."}],["$","$L1a",null,{"children":["\n",["$","p",null,{"children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":"Who this is for:"}]," anyone whose build is measured in thousands of actions and\ntens of minutes, on hardware that isn't uniform. ",["$","strong",null,{"children":"What you'll have at the end:"}],"\nan understanding of why these builds are the hard case, and how Forge routes\nactions to the machines that suit them. ",["$","strong",null,{"children":"Time:"}]," about fifteen minutes."]}],"\n",["$","$L1b",null,{"as":"h2","id":"what-makes-a-build-large-in-the-way-that-matters","children":"What makes a build \"large\" in the way that matters"}],"\n",["$","p",null,{"children":"Size in gigabytes is not the interesting axis. Three properties are, and a build\nthat has all three is the shape remote execution was designed around."}],"\n",["$","p",null,{"children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":"Action count."}]," An EDA flow (synthesis, place-and-route, timing, DRC, LVS)\nor a full LLVM tree is tens of thousands of actions. At that count the graph is\nwide enough that the number of cores you can throw at it is the only thing\nsetting the wall clock. A laptop has sixteen. A worker pool has however many you\nask for."]}],"\n",["$","p",null,{"children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":"Heterogeneity."}]," The actions are not interchangeable. A link step wants a\nmachine with a great deal of memory and will use one core doing it. A thousand\ncompiles want a thousand cores and very little memory each. A simulation wants a\nGPU. A vendor tool wants a specific OS, sometimes a specific kernel, and a\nlicense seat. Sizing one machine for all of that means sizing it for the worst\ncase and wasting it on every other action."]}],"\n",["$","p",null,{"children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":"The long tail."}]," Large graphs have a critical path, and near the end of the\nbuild most of the fleet is idle while a handful of long actions finish. The\ntotal is set by the longest chain, not by the sum of the work. That's why \"add\nmore cores\" stops helping at a point, and why ",["$","em",null,{"children":"which"}]," machine runs the long\nactions matters more than how many machines you have."]}],"\n",["$","$L1b",null,{"as":"h2","id":"why-caching-alone-runs-out","children":"Why caching alone runs out"}],"\n",["$","p",null,{"children":"On a small build, the cache is most of the story. On a build like this it is\nstill enormously valuable (it is still the thing you deploy first, and Getting\nstarted is still where to start), but it stops being sufficient, for a specific reason."}],"\n","$L1c","\n","$L1d","\n","$L1e","\n","$L1f","\n","$L20","\n","$L21","\n","$L22","\n","$L23","\n","$L24","\n","$L25","\n","$L26","\n","$L27","\n","$L28","\n","$L29","\n","$L2a","\n","$L2b","\n","$L2c","\n","$L2d","\n","$L2e","\n","$L2f","\n","$L30","\n","$L31","\n","$L32","\n","$L33","\n","$L34","\n","$L35","\n","$L36","\n","$L37","\n","$L38","\n","$L39","\n","$L3a","\n","$L3b","\n","$L3c","\n","$L3d","\n","$L3e","\n","$L3f","\n","$L40","\n","$L41","\n","$L42","\n","$L43"]}],"$L44"]}]
